(c) “full-blood” and “half-blood” two person are said to be related to each other by fullblood when they are descended from a common ancestor by the same wife and by half 
blood when they are descended from a common ancestor but by different wives ; 
(d) “uterine blood”- two persons are said to be related to each other by uterine blood 
when they are descended from a common ancestress but by different husbands; 
Explanation :- in clauses (c) and (d) ancestor includes the father and ancestress the 
mother; 
